1
00:00:18,321 --> 00:00:20,615
"To Ms. Anzu Hoshino."

2
00:00:20,699 --> 00:00:21,700
PRODUCT TYPE: VIDEO GAME

3
00:00:21,783 --> 00:00:24,119
Hooray! It's finally here!

4
00:00:25,245 --> 00:00:28,874
My entire purpose in life
is right here in my hands!

5
00:00:29,875 --> 00:00:30,959
Look at this!

6
00:00:31,043 --> 00:00:32,711
Ever since elementary school,

7
00:00:32,794 --> 00:00:34,963
I spent my time
playing games with the boys.

8
00:00:36,381 --> 00:00:37,299
In junior high…

9
00:00:37,382 --> 00:00:39,468
Hey, karaoke tonight?

10
00:00:39,551 --> 00:00:41,386
Beating the final boss
was more important

11
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:44,306
than hanging out with boys.

12
00:00:45,724 --> 00:00:47,893
-Whoa, are you really eating all that?
-Huh?

13
00:00:47,976 --> 00:00:50,145
Won't you gain weight?
And you'll break out.

14
00:00:51,146 --> 00:00:54,441
I don't care what anyone says,
chocolate is my life!

15
00:00:54,524 --> 00:00:56,359
NOPE, DON'T EAT THEM
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT, GOBBLE IT DOWN

16
00:00:57,194 --> 00:00:58,779
I love you!

17
00:00:58,862 --> 00:01:02,449
But the love of my life is Momohiki!

18
00:01:02,532 --> 00:01:03,867
CUDDLE MOMOHIKI
KISS MOMOHIKI

19
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:07,871
Romance was non-existent in my life until…

20
00:01:12,459 --> 00:01:14,753
Why… Why am I…

21
00:01:16,838 --> 00:01:18,340
…yuka-don-ing this hottie?

22
00:03:00,984 --> 00:03:03,069
I get to play my video game

23
00:03:03,153 --> 00:03:04,321
all weekend long.

24
00:03:04,404 --> 00:03:08,909
Yeah! All-nighter, let's do this!

25
00:03:13,997 --> 00:03:15,165
Aah…

26
00:03:15,248 --> 00:03:18,418
Huh? Did they change the opening a bit?

27
00:03:19,336 --> 00:03:23,632
Ah, whatever! Start button!

28
00:03:27,219 --> 00:03:29,638
Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

29
00:03:35,143 --> 00:03:36,353
Oh!

30
00:03:41,441 --> 00:03:43,777
What the heck is with this terrible game?

31
00:03:44,569 --> 00:03:47,781
Oh, come on,
this has to be the wrong game!

32
00:03:48,823 --> 00:03:50,033
Hm?

33
00:03:55,538 --> 00:03:56,915
A fanfare, please!

34
00:03:57,582 --> 00:04:00,418
You've been selected today as subject one.

35
00:04:00,502 --> 00:04:02,379
So, congratulations!

36
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:07,342
Hello! I'm Riri, the wizard,
who grants all of your dreams.

37
00:04:07,425 --> 00:04:08,927
What? A wizard?

38
00:04:09,469 --> 00:04:11,513
-It's complicated to explain…
-Hm.

39
00:04:11,596 --> 00:04:15,058
…so for the time being,
please, just read this carefully.

40
00:04:16,142 --> 00:04:18,603
What's up with all this legalese
in a magic-themed game?

41
00:04:18,687 --> 00:04:20,522
-And it goes on forever!
-Ugh…

42
00:04:20,605 --> 00:04:23,108
Can you just explain it
in a few sentences?

43
00:04:23,191 --> 00:04:24,526
You mean like this?

44
00:04:24,609 --> 00:04:27,279
No! Just give me a brief summary.

45
00:04:27,362 --> 00:04:29,322
Well, to put it simply,

46
00:04:29,406 --> 00:04:31,449
we came all the way from the Magic World…

47
00:04:31,533 --> 00:04:35,829
…to support those with no experience
with romantic relationships like you.

48
00:04:35,912 --> 00:04:36,913
Count me out.

49
00:04:36,997 --> 00:04:40,458
So, when did your heart
last throb for a guy?

50
00:04:40,542 --> 00:04:45,463
Oh… Like with Lord Matthew
and Swordsman Musashimaru?

51
00:04:45,547 --> 00:04:47,966
Those are games characters, right?

52
00:04:48,049 --> 00:04:52,345
You're in high school, it's time
to quit dreaming and face reality.

53
00:04:52,429 --> 00:04:54,973
Aren't you the wizard
who's supposed to grant my dreams?

54
00:04:55,056 --> 00:04:56,474
But…

55
00:04:56,558 --> 00:04:58,935
I'm here now, there's no need to worry.

56
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:03,690
I'm here to grant girls like you,
who rejects all opportunities of romance,

57
00:05:03,773 --> 00:05:06,943
a chance to experience love
through this dating game

58
00:05:07,027 --> 00:05:08,320
Dating game!

59
00:05:08,403 --> 00:05:09,446
-Sorry.
-Dating game!

60
00:05:09,529 --> 00:05:12,449
I'm not understanding
a word that you're saying.

61
00:05:12,532 --> 00:05:16,119
It seems to me you have no problem
with those dating games

62
00:05:16,202 --> 00:05:19,581
as long as they're made for women.
Isn't that right, huh?

63
00:05:20,081 --> 00:05:21,458
Hmm, sure…

64
00:05:22,167 --> 00:05:28,465
Well then, as the selected test subject,
you'll get to enjoy living your life

65
00:05:28,548 --> 00:05:32,510
just like the heroine
of the game I programmed,

66
00:05:32,594 --> 00:05:34,971
Romantic Thriller!

67
00:05:35,055 --> 00:05:37,807
Did you watch the lovely opening sequence?

68
00:05:37,891 --> 00:05:39,642
And for you, Anzu,

69
00:05:40,143 --> 00:05:42,562
your romance experience scores at zero

70
00:05:42,645 --> 00:05:44,689
so it may have been too intense.

71
00:05:44,773 --> 00:05:46,191
No, I just knew I was playing…

72
00:05:46,274 --> 00:05:49,819
…a terrible game with total amateur
writing and production value.

73
00:05:49,903 --> 00:05:52,697
Ah, so you're particular
about the virtual world

74
00:05:52,781 --> 00:05:54,657
despite having no romantic experiences

75
00:05:54,741 --> 00:05:56,242
-in reality.
-Of course! Do you have any idea

76
00:05:56,326 --> 00:05:58,286
how many dating games I've finished?

77
00:05:58,370 --> 00:06:00,872
But imagine
if you could experience life

78
00:06:00,955 --> 00:06:03,708
surrounded by hot guys for real
just like in the dating game,

79
00:06:03,792 --> 00:06:06,836
even your heart would flutter
with excitement, don't you think?

80
00:06:07,462 --> 00:06:09,297
In-- In real life?

81
00:06:09,381 --> 00:06:10,340
That's right.

82
00:06:10,423 --> 00:06:11,674
In real life.

83
00:06:12,258 --> 00:06:14,177
A super normie life

84
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:16,679
filled with ago-kui…

85
00:06:16,763 --> 00:06:20,850
Lots of kissing and kabe-don awaits you!

86
00:06:20,934 --> 00:06:23,561
-Re-- Really?
-Yes, really!

87
00:06:24,104 --> 00:06:29,359
All kinds of serious hotties agree
to start appearing around you.

88
00:06:29,442 --> 00:06:32,570
And you're gonna be oh so busy!

89
00:06:32,654 --> 00:06:33,947
That many guys?

90
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:38,118
You see, Anzu? Aren't you beginning
to see me as an angel?

91
00:06:38,201 --> 00:06:41,621
But, no, I already have
the love of my life, Momohiki!

92
00:06:41,704 --> 00:06:43,415
Wait! Where is he?

93
00:06:43,498 --> 00:06:46,376
Momohiki! Huh! Oh! Momohiki?

94
00:06:46,459 --> 00:06:50,755
Ahem. To keep you focus
on your romantic relationships,

95
00:06:50,839 --> 00:06:54,592
your favorite video games, chocolate,
your cat, your three greatest desires

96
00:06:54,676 --> 00:06:57,011
have all been confiscated by yours truly.

97
00:06:57,095 --> 00:06:58,888
Confiscated?

98
00:06:58,972 --> 00:07:01,808
Are you kidding? Come on! There's no way.

99
00:07:04,394 --> 00:07:07,230
No!

100
00:07:08,189 --> 00:07:10,108
Huh?

101
00:07:10,191 --> 00:07:11,276
See?

102
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,161
All… All of my games

103
00:07:21,244 --> 00:07:25,498
have turned into
Kabayaki-chan Goro snacks!

104
00:07:25,582 --> 00:07:28,835
And look,
it's the "soft" kind, too.

105
00:07:29,377 --> 00:07:30,253
Not funny at all!

106
00:07:30,837 --> 00:07:32,380
What about my chocolate?

107
00:07:34,841 --> 00:07:37,010
What? Oh, no!

108
00:07:37,093 --> 00:07:39,012
There's no chocolate on anything!

109
00:07:39,095 --> 00:07:41,890
The delicious parts are all totally gone!

110
00:07:43,016 --> 00:07:44,517
Confiscated.

111
00:07:44,601 --> 00:07:48,605
Eating too much chocolate is bad
for your skin and it's a lot of fat.

112
00:07:48,688 --> 00:07:51,274
Don't say that
while you're covered in chocolate!

113
00:07:51,357 --> 00:07:53,318
So now do you understand what it means…

114
00:07:53,401 --> 00:07:55,570
…to eliminate your three greatest desires?

115
00:07:55,653 --> 00:07:56,488
Monster!

116
00:07:56,571 --> 00:08:00,700
If you want to gain something,
you have to pay the price.

117
00:08:00,783 --> 00:08:02,243
Did you think you'll get a paradise…

118
00:08:02,327 --> 00:08:05,538
…of hotties for free?
Don't be ridiculous! Come on!

119
00:08:05,622 --> 00:08:06,789
You devil!

120
00:08:06,873 --> 00:08:09,250
Hey! Please, watch your mouth.

121
00:08:09,334 --> 00:08:13,087
To be honest with you, I'm just
your everyday gentle-hearted wizard.

122
00:08:13,671 --> 00:08:16,424
I'm saying this
with your best interest at heart.

123
00:08:16,508 --> 00:08:19,511
What is this? Brainwashing?
Some sketchy cult?

124
00:08:19,594 --> 00:08:24,349
This is the only way that'll get you
to prioritize cuties over your cat.

125
00:08:24,432 --> 00:08:26,935
Ugh…

126
00:08:27,018 --> 00:08:28,394
When you get lonely,

127
00:08:28,478 --> 00:08:31,731
you most likely turn to chocolates
instead of a boyfriend.

128
00:08:32,774 --> 00:08:35,109
Instead of setting aside time for dates,

129
00:08:35,193 --> 00:08:37,111
you spend all your time playing games.

130
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,448
So now, do you get it?

131
00:08:40,532 --> 00:08:44,452
How toxic your three greatest desires are
for romantic relationships?

132
00:08:44,536 --> 00:08:48,540
They will be confiscated indefinitely
until you achieve

133
00:08:48,623 --> 00:08:52,126
a lovely Romantic Thriller-level
relationship!

134
00:08:52,210 --> 00:08:53,044
FOREVER CONFISCATED

135
00:08:53,127 --> 00:08:54,921
Impossible! Riri!

136
00:08:55,964 --> 00:08:58,967
I can't even handle
a day without them!

137
00:08:59,050 --> 00:09:01,219
I can live without guys, okay?

138
00:09:01,302 --> 00:09:05,557
But my three greatest desires
are a total necessity for me!

139
00:09:06,182 --> 00:09:08,393
That's exactly why you were chosen.

140
00:09:08,476 --> 00:09:09,644
Like I said,

141
00:09:09,727 --> 00:09:14,440
we are here to solve Japan's extremely
serious low birth rate problem.

142
00:09:14,524 --> 00:09:16,776
Low birth rate?
That's what this is all about?

143
00:09:16,859 --> 00:09:19,028
Look at that.
You didn't read the explanation

144
00:09:19,112 --> 00:09:21,531
in the beginning carefully.

145
00:09:22,365 --> 00:09:23,241
Either way,

146
00:09:23,324 --> 00:09:26,035
I'll be assisting you
with your romantic relationships

147
00:09:26,119 --> 00:09:27,495
as best as I can.

148
00:09:27,579 --> 00:09:32,458
For love, for the future of Japan,
and most importantly, for my salary!

149
00:09:32,542 --> 00:09:34,877
Keep that last part
to yourself, all right?

150
00:09:34,961 --> 00:09:36,713
-Oh, my goodness!
-Huh?

151
00:09:36,796 --> 00:09:39,799
I forgot that I left the stove on earlier.

152
00:09:39,882 --> 00:09:42,677
Well, time to go back to the Magic World.

153
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:45,054
I am not getting involved with this!

154
00:09:45,138 --> 00:09:47,181
Actually, remember hitting
your start button before?

155
00:09:47,265 --> 00:09:49,517
Too late! There's no turning back

156
00:09:49,601 --> 00:09:52,020
even if it feels like
sailing a boat made of mud.

157
00:09:52,103 --> 00:09:53,438
No way! A mud boat!

158
00:09:53,521 --> 00:09:55,940
Come on, it was only a little joke.

159
00:09:56,024 --> 00:09:59,819
In reality, an exciting,
Titaniclevel romance awaits you!

160
00:09:59,902 --> 00:10:02,947
Either way, the boat is sinking.

161
00:10:03,031 --> 00:10:06,826
Life without my three greatest desires
is gonna be miserable.

162
00:10:06,909 --> 00:10:09,203
Give me back my reason to live!

163
00:10:09,287 --> 00:10:11,831
Until next time! Bon voyage!

164
00:10:11,914 --> 00:10:13,875
Wait a sec! Hey! Wait!

165
00:10:16,377 --> 00:10:18,129
-Mom! Where's Momohiki?
-Huh?

166
00:10:18,212 --> 00:10:20,757
Hm, he's right over there.

167
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:23,259
Why the heck is he up there?

168
00:10:23,343 --> 00:10:26,387
Momohiki, please, please, please,
show me your cute face!

169
00:10:28,222 --> 00:10:29,307
I'm home!

170
00:10:29,390 --> 00:10:30,224
Huh?

171
00:10:31,267 --> 00:10:33,519
Oh, you're home early.

172
00:10:33,603 --> 00:10:35,688
Yeah. I know this is sudden…

173
00:10:35,772 --> 00:10:36,773
Momohiki, please…

174
00:10:36,856 --> 00:10:39,484
…but it's been decided
that I'll be transferred to the US.

175
00:10:39,567 --> 00:10:40,943
-Wow!
-What?

176
00:10:41,944 --> 00:10:43,863
And I want you to come with me.

177
00:10:43,946 --> 00:10:47,367
It's always been
a dream of mine to live overseas.

178
00:10:48,284 --> 00:10:50,328
Wait! What about me?

179
00:10:50,411 --> 00:10:52,330
Anzu, honey, you have school.

180
00:10:52,413 --> 00:10:53,706
It will only be two
or three years.

181
00:10:53,790 --> 00:10:54,624
-What?
-You should be able

182
00:10:54,707 --> 00:10:56,876
-to hold down the fort yourself by now.
-Mm-hmm.

183
00:10:56,959 --> 00:10:59,796
-We'll take Momohiki with us too.
-Wait! Things are happening too fast!

184
00:11:00,463 --> 00:11:04,550
And Dad, aren't you
a post office employee?

185
00:11:04,634 --> 00:11:06,928
Why is the relocation, seriously?

186
00:11:07,845 --> 00:11:09,681
We should get started packing right away.

187
00:11:09,764 --> 00:11:11,766
And we should also celebrate tonight.

188
00:11:16,104 --> 00:11:17,522
All right then, we're off.

189
00:11:17,605 --> 00:11:20,942
Make sure you eat every day.
And keep all the doors locked.

190
00:11:21,025 --> 00:11:23,069
Take care!

191
00:11:26,406 --> 00:11:29,409
It took them no time to pack
and they're moving overseas.

192
00:11:29,492 --> 00:11:32,370
Mom and Dad
were much too casual about this,

193
00:11:32,453 --> 00:11:34,664
and their whole
high-schooler-living-alone-thing

194
00:11:34,747 --> 00:11:36,457
is way too forced!

195
00:11:37,291 --> 00:11:40,753
Well, I had to establish
the playing field early on.

196
00:11:51,723 --> 00:11:54,559
That's right. I've got
extra energy because I'm mad

197
00:11:54,642 --> 00:11:56,519
and you better watch out!

198
00:11:56,602 --> 00:11:57,854
I expect nothing less.

199
00:11:57,937 --> 00:12:01,023
You're the anti-heroine type,
I recognized.

200
00:12:01,107 --> 00:12:02,817
NON-HEROINE

201
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:05,862
I don't care what you call me…

202
00:12:05,945 --> 00:12:07,864
…just turn things back to normal now.

203
00:12:07,947 --> 00:12:10,366
Give me back Momohiki!

204
00:12:10,450 --> 00:12:11,284
Impossible!

205
00:12:16,539 --> 00:12:19,083
Damn it!

206
00:12:19,167 --> 00:12:20,376
Are you kidding me?

207
00:12:20,877 --> 00:12:22,795
-Chocolate!
-Oh, sorry.

208
00:12:22,879 --> 00:12:24,797
-Chocolate!
-We're closed today.

209
00:12:24,881 --> 00:12:25,715
Where's the chocolate!

210
00:12:25,798 --> 00:12:27,425
We're having
a sugar-free snack fair.

211
00:12:27,508 --> 00:12:29,427
ON SALE
MANAGER'S CHOICE

212
00:12:30,094 --> 00:12:31,012
For real?

213
00:12:32,638 --> 00:12:34,974
They're all sold out? Is that a thing?

214
00:12:36,434 --> 00:12:41,981
Am I cursed to never eat chocolate
ever again in my whole entire life? Ever?

215
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:46,486
The chocolate… The cacao…
I'm getting withdrawals…

216
00:12:47,278 --> 00:12:49,739
Why is this happening?

217
00:12:49,822 --> 00:12:52,825
You're kidding me!

218
00:12:53,326 --> 00:12:56,037
Am I really gonna let
that thing who created

219
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,790
that awful Romantic Thriller game
tell me what to do?

220
00:13:02,168 --> 00:13:04,378
No way! Not a chance!

221
00:13:04,462 --> 00:13:08,299
Even if a hot guy does show up,
I just won't fall in love, right?

222
00:13:08,382 --> 00:13:11,010
I'm sorry, but there's no way
someone exists in real life

223
00:13:11,093 --> 00:13:12,470
who could surpass the high standards

224
00:13:12,553 --> 00:13:14,931
I've set up after my experiences
with 2D guys.

225
00:13:16,516 --> 00:13:19,268
As long as
no romantic relationship develops,

226
00:13:19,352 --> 00:13:22,063
then that thing will have no choice…

227
00:13:22,146 --> 00:13:24,774
…but to give up and leave me alone!

228
00:13:28,319 --> 00:13:32,240
Sneaky devil who stole
my three greatest desires!

229
00:13:32,824 --> 00:13:36,244
Yes,  Romantic Thriller, you say?

230
00:13:36,327 --> 00:13:38,246
I will destroy it all.

231
00:13:38,329 --> 00:13:42,416
And I will become the Romantic Killer!

232
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:51,259
That being said,
bring it on you so-called cuties!

233
00:13:54,345 --> 00:13:56,097
Oh.

234
00:13:58,182 --> 00:13:59,183
Aah!

235
00:13:59,267 --> 00:14:01,561
I am so sorry!

236
00:14:03,688 --> 00:14:05,064
That's a pretty good crack.

237
00:14:06,566 --> 00:14:09,026
Wow, a hot guy
actually showed up.

238
00:14:10,111 --> 00:14:13,239
I'm really sorry! I'll pay to fix it.

239
00:14:13,322 --> 00:14:15,616
You don't have
to pay for the repairs.

240
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:16,617
What?

241
00:14:16,701 --> 00:14:19,495
I wasn't paying attention either.

242
00:14:22,707 --> 00:14:27,003
He's nothing compared to
Matthew and Musashimaru!

243
00:14:28,588 --> 00:14:31,591
Well, then, uh, thanks! Thanks a lot!

244
00:14:31,674 --> 00:14:34,969
I'm sorry I bumped you. Goodbye!

245
00:14:37,638 --> 00:14:39,265
Uh-- Uh…

246
00:14:45,771 --> 00:14:47,607
I'm off to school.

247
00:14:50,902 --> 00:14:54,280
Not like there's anyone home to hear me.

248
00:14:56,490 --> 00:15:00,161
I can't believe I ran into
that adorable guy yesterday.

249
00:15:01,454 --> 00:15:05,791
But as long as I avoid
getting involved, it's all good, right?

250
00:15:05,875 --> 00:15:07,418
Just wait and see, devil!

251
00:15:07,501 --> 00:15:10,046
-Good morning to you!
-They're back!

252
00:15:10,129 --> 00:15:12,798
All right.
Time to march on into school.

253
00:15:15,426 --> 00:15:16,427
Wait! What?

254
00:15:23,684 --> 00:15:25,728
Why are you following me, huh?

255
00:15:25,811 --> 00:15:29,857
Not to worry, no one but you can see me.

256
00:15:29,941 --> 00:15:32,151
Exactly. That's what I'm worried about.

257
00:15:32,234 --> 00:15:35,363
I'll look crazy if people think
that I'm talking to myself.

258
00:15:35,446 --> 00:15:37,615
Don't worry about that, either.

259
00:15:37,698 --> 00:15:42,620
Whenever you're talking to me,
everyone else is seeing an illusion.

260
00:15:42,703 --> 00:15:43,955
So they won't notice.

261
00:15:44,038 --> 00:15:46,916
You're so annoying.
I'll probably just ignore you.

262
00:15:46,999 --> 00:15:48,960
However, young lady…

263
00:15:58,552 --> 00:16:01,305
You must not underestimate my magic.

264
00:16:01,389 --> 00:16:04,016
But, come on!
That wasn't really magic at all!

265
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:06,018
I'm off before you take revenge.

266
00:16:08,521 --> 00:16:10,314
Huh?

267
00:16:10,398 --> 00:16:13,234
It's that hottie from yesterday?

268
00:16:15,611 --> 00:16:17,697
That uniform… No way!

269
00:16:18,781 --> 00:16:21,200
We go to the same school?

270
00:16:21,784 --> 00:16:22,743
That little devil!

271
00:16:22,827 --> 00:16:24,161
Are you okay, dear?

272
00:16:24,245 --> 00:16:28,249
I'm sorry. I'm such a total klutz.

273
00:16:28,332 --> 00:16:30,501
Riri set me up for that meeting.

274
00:16:32,795 --> 00:16:34,797
Huh? You okay? What happened?

275
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:38,926
Jeez, Tsukasa,
don't just stand there, give her a hand.

276
00:16:40,428 --> 00:16:42,471
Oh, that's okay. I'm totally fine!

277
00:16:42,555 --> 00:16:44,849
I'm not gonna let that thing
have their way.

278
00:16:47,476 --> 00:16:48,310
Uh…

279
00:16:51,939 --> 00:16:52,982
S-- See ya.

280
00:16:54,692 --> 00:16:57,194
Big deal, he ignored me too.

281
00:17:04,452 --> 00:17:06,954
-Oh, hey, here he comes. Look!
-Excuse me.

282
00:17:07,496 --> 00:17:09,123
You've been on my mind.

283
00:17:11,083 --> 00:17:13,294
Here you go.
Will you please read my letter?

284
00:17:14,295 --> 00:17:16,422
Oh, a girl's confessing
her love to him.

285
00:17:16,505 --> 00:17:17,798
Typical life of a hot guy.

286
00:17:19,341 --> 00:17:20,468
That was really brave of her.

287
00:17:20,551 --> 00:17:21,385
I don't want it.

288
00:17:23,054 --> 00:17:24,889
What? Uh, uh…

289
00:17:25,514 --> 00:17:26,432
Uh…

290
00:17:26,515 --> 00:17:28,976
I'm sorry about him.

291
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:30,019
Ouch.

292
00:17:30,102 --> 00:17:31,520
That poor girl.

293
00:17:31,604 --> 00:17:32,980
Hey, what was that?

294
00:17:33,064 --> 00:17:35,691
He's cute, but his personality?
Not so much.

295
00:17:35,775 --> 00:17:38,360
Hey, Tsukasa. Good morning.

296
00:17:38,444 --> 00:17:40,488
I saw that. But I do get it.

297
00:17:41,155 --> 00:17:45,576
A letter is just a little bit extra
these days, don't you think so?

298
00:17:45,659 --> 00:17:48,079
Really? I'd be flattered
if I got a letter.

299
00:17:48,162 --> 00:17:50,873
I mean, you should've
at least accepted it from her.

300
00:17:53,042 --> 00:17:55,044
I don't want her to get
the wrong idea from me.

301
00:17:55,628 --> 00:17:56,962
I understand.

302
00:17:57,046 --> 00:17:58,589
She's not your type, right?

303
00:17:58,672 --> 00:18:02,301
Ugh! He's full of himself
just because he's a little popular.

304
00:18:02,384 --> 00:18:04,845
There's no way I'd date a guy like him!

305
00:18:04,929 --> 00:18:08,641
But anyway, I sent you a message
yesterday and you didn't even read it.

306
00:18:08,724 --> 00:18:10,017
My phone broke.

307
00:18:14,814 --> 00:18:16,816
-That blows.
-Do you have insurance?

308
00:18:16,899 --> 00:18:18,526
I was cheap, I didn't get it.

309
00:18:18,609 --> 00:18:19,985
Seriously? That sucks!

310
00:18:20,069 --> 00:18:22,488
I'd die without my phone.

311
00:18:22,571 --> 00:18:24,824
Aren you gonna buy a new one?

312
00:18:24,907 --> 00:18:27,284
Not for a while. I can't afford it.

313
00:18:27,368 --> 00:18:28,786
Really?

314
00:18:32,373 --> 00:18:33,249
Whoa.

315
00:18:33,332 --> 00:18:36,252
Your dad was transferred
to the US out of nowhere?

316
00:18:36,836 --> 00:18:37,753
Yeah,

317
00:18:37,837 --> 00:18:40,756
that's the reason why I didn't have
any time to make my lunch today.

318
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:43,634
Sorry to drag you here with me, Saki.

319
00:18:43,717 --> 00:18:46,554
No worries.
It's my first time here. I'm excited.

320
00:18:46,637 --> 00:18:49,890
Right? Now let's see,
what should I eat?

321
00:18:50,516 --> 00:18:52,101
I'll order for both of us.

322
00:18:52,643 --> 00:18:54,395
All right, the decision is made.

323
00:18:54,478 --> 00:18:55,813
Uh, I'll get…

324
00:18:56,397 --> 00:18:57,523
Lunch set A.

325
00:19:05,489 --> 00:19:08,367
I think he's the hot guy
that everyone's been talking about.

326
00:19:08,450 --> 00:19:10,327
Kazuki from Class 7.

327
00:19:10,995 --> 00:19:12,079
Kazuki?

328
00:19:13,247 --> 00:19:14,331
I see.

329
00:19:14,415 --> 00:19:17,251
Yeah. And he's really popular
with all the girls.

330
00:19:17,334 --> 00:19:19,253
You probably didn't notice

331
00:19:19,336 --> 00:19:21,964
because you're usually busy
playing your video games during lunch

332
00:19:25,968 --> 00:19:28,679
I heard he moved here alone
from another prefecture.

333
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,473
Apparently, the girls like him
because he's reserved

334
00:19:31,557 --> 00:19:34,101
-and doesn't smile much.
-I see.

335
00:19:34,185 --> 00:19:35,269
I don't want it.

336
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:38,564
I don't want her
to get the wrong idea from me.

337
00:19:39,231 --> 00:19:41,066
He's reserved, huh?

338
00:19:41,150 --> 00:19:43,986
I'd say he's got some personality issues

339
00:19:44,069 --> 00:19:48,908
Slowly falling in love after a terrible
first impression is a classic scenario.

340
00:19:48,991 --> 00:19:49,825
Shut up!

341
00:19:52,369 --> 00:19:54,538
-Time to eat.
-Tsukasa!

342
00:19:54,622 --> 00:19:56,874
I'm gonna sit next to you.

343
00:19:57,750 --> 00:20:01,003
Oh. So, hey, I heard
you live all by yourself.

344
00:20:01,086 --> 00:20:05,633
That's nuts. I wanna come and hang out.
Where do you live?

345
00:20:05,716 --> 00:20:08,510
Ugh! I'm not listening!
Not listening! No!

346
00:20:09,595 --> 00:20:12,765
I gotta shut out
all the information I don't want to know!

347
00:20:12,848 --> 00:20:15,976
I gotta avoid going to the cafeteria
as much as possible.

348
00:20:20,773 --> 00:20:22,775
There's nothing to do here!

349
00:20:23,442 --> 00:20:24,318
I'm bored.

350
00:20:27,446 --> 00:20:30,699
How do people live without gaming?

351
00:20:31,617 --> 00:20:35,120
Momohiki is gone and there's no chocolate.

352
00:20:41,794 --> 00:20:44,046
Time to make dinner.

353
00:20:55,599 --> 00:20:59,144
Roaches are unseemly,
so instead, cake. You're welcome!

354
00:21:02,064 --> 00:21:02,898
THE GLASS IS IMAGINARY

355
00:21:02,982 --> 00:21:05,484
Mommy!

356
00:21:10,447 --> 00:21:14,076
Oh, that's right!
I lost my extermination expert!

357
00:21:14,159 --> 00:21:16,120
She would get rid of them for me.

358
00:21:21,208 --> 00:21:25,129
It's time to awaken
the soldier within me!

359
00:21:27,673 --> 00:21:29,133
Go!

360
00:21:32,428 --> 00:21:34,471
Damn, it's empty!

361
00:21:52,865 --> 00:21:55,826
I rushed out,
I didn't bring anything with me.

362
00:21:55,909 --> 00:21:58,287
And I'm wearing two different shoes.

363
00:21:58,370 --> 00:22:01,623
I don't want to go home,
but I'm seriously starving.

364
00:22:02,416 --> 00:22:04,418
Mommy.

365
00:22:09,673 --> 00:22:11,717
Ugh! This is the worst!

366
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:13,677
I need to take cover somewhere.

367
00:22:28,192 --> 00:22:30,277
And it's pouring.

368
00:22:42,748 --> 00:22:43,582
Huh?

369
00:22:48,921 --> 00:22:49,922
Uh…

370
00:22:53,008 --> 00:22:54,551
A fanfare, please!

371
00:22:54,635 --> 00:22:56,720
And a big congratulations!

372
00:22:56,804 --> 00:22:58,722
Did you fall for my little trick?

373
00:22:58,806 --> 00:23:02,226
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

374
00:23:02,309 --> 00:23:05,896
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

375
00:23:05,979 --> 00:23:08,649
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

376
00:23:08,732 --> 00:23:11,026
Don't just let things be! Come on!

377
00:23:11,110 --> 00:23:13,695
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

378
00:23:13,779 --> 00:23:15,697
So I can make sure I get paid.

